cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "hazus-curves: an open database of FEMA Hazus damage and vulnerability curves"
message: >-
  If you use this database, please cite both this repository and the underlying
  FEMA Hazus model and its originating agencies. The curves are FEMA's work;
  this project only extracts, reshapes and documents them.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Vaughn
    given-names: Ryan
version: 0.1.0
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Tidy, long-format relational database of FEMA Hazus flood depth-damage functions
  (Hazus 4.0 and 6.1) and hurricane wind damage and loss functions (Hazus 6.1),
  extracted from public sources, with full per-value provenance, a measured
  version diff, and independent verification of a FEMA-disclosed data defect.
keywords:
  - Hazus
  - FEMA
  - natural hazards
  - flood
  - hurricane
  - vulnerability functions
  - depth-damage functions

references:
  - type: software
    title: "Hazus"
    authors:
      - name: "Federal Emergency Management Agency"
    notes: >-
      Underlying source of all curve data. Flood curves in this database are from
      Hazus 4.0 and 6.1; hurricane curves are from Hazus 6.1. Cite the specific
      Hazus version and technical manual relevant to your use. Originating
      agencies named in the source_agency field include US Army Corps of Engineers
      districts, the Federal Insurance Administration, and FEMA's Benefit-Cost
      Analysis and Probabilistic Flood Risk Assessment programmes.
    url: "https://www.fema.gov/flood-maps/products-tools/hazus"
  - type: software
    title: "FAST (Flood Assessment Structure Tool)"
    authors:
      - name: "Federal Emergency Management Agency"
    notes: "Source of the Hazus 4.0 flood damage function tables."
    url: "https://github.com/nhrap-hazus/FAST"
  - type: software
    title: "physrisk"
    authors:
      - name: "OS-Climate"
    notes: >-
      Maintains the public bucket from which the Hazus 6.1 flood and hurricane
      workbooks were obtained.
    url: "https://github.com/os-climate/physrisk"
